{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375238-archpillars-dark-age-archmages","id":1375238,"title":"ArchPillars? Dark Age Archmages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-17T01:34:03-07:00","id":1375238,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> ArchPillars? Dark Age Archmages","content":"Idea I never see brought up surprisingly is Archmages of the Pillar Foundation Variety. Now I know you can say they don't exist but humor me for the case of this thread. So we know Archmages were hundreds of years old if not Thousands, and that would mean the older ones would have not relied on Spheres, but for the sake of sanity for the ST, and because Dark Age Mage wasn't invented till later, they just had the Archmages use spheres.<br /> <br /> But what if we made the older Archmages with the Pillar Foundation Rule? Anyone have any idea for Archpillars? You can go with the single level 6 Archpillar idea, or the 6-10 idea.<br /> <br /> And what about Oracles before their were Spheres? This possibly could lead to the idea maybe even in prehistoric time maybe a secret group of mages did use spheres, like maybe Sphere mages is a legacy of when Demons tried to enlighten man in the Babel Project. Or it represents what Adam and Eve passed on to the brood of Seth, and Pillars are actually divergent from that leading to a period of history before Spheres were rediscovered. Or not whatever just spitballing here.<br /> <br /> But I'm interested in ideas and discussion. The Black Hand could have Pillar Archmage Liches using their Funky Loka Pillars.<br /> <br /> What are some thoughts on Pillar Mages interacting with Sphere mages, that was always an idea I had running in my head to explore someday. Like when spheres were pioneered and taught to the next generation what about say playing the last generation of Pillar mages before spheres got standardized so part of the Group uses Pillars and part use spheres. Any ideas on rules for how they interact?<br /> <br /> I just love the idea of before the fall of Horizon and all those umbral Chantry Realms we had old Wizards of the Fellowships each having joined different Tradition. After all depending on individual Philosophy you could have a Valderman who joined the Verbena Focusing on Blood and tradition, while his Cabal Mate chose to join the Celestial Chorus focusing on his faith to the gods of old.<br /> <br /> Its ripe for ideas, even if it doesn't belong in every chronicle.<br /> <br /> Hell Black Hand shows how it can make sense for mage groups on the Periphery, isolated as they are, kept Pillars even in modern day. I love that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T04:51:15-07:00","id":1375258,"title":"","content":"A resource, but from a VDA20 book<br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">P74, Tome of Secrets</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An Awakened witch possesses a Foundation rating of 1\u20135 dots (though a few legendary figures may possess ratings of 6 or higher) and one to four Pillars, also rated at 1\u20135 dots (again, legends may possess higher ratings, similar to vampire elders). </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But again, I suspect if the author has full understanding of DAM, Pillar system is very different from Spheres' and Disciplines'</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 03-17-2020, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T04:52:13-07:00","id":1376517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375238-archpillars-dark-age-archmages?p=1375258#post1375258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A resource, but from a VDA20 book<br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">P74, Tome of Secrets</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But again, I suspect if the author has full understanding of DAM, Pillar system is very different from Spheres' and Disciplines'</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>So I'm super curious about the legends of Archpillars then!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T08:58:31-07:00","id":1376562,"title":"","content":"The Foundation and Pillars system as described in V20 Dark Ages is a hack that's built on the framework of Vampire's Disciplines: <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">\u201cA witch can use any Discipline (not just blood magic) that would fall under a Pillar that she knows, limited to the dot rating in that Pillar. Instead of the listed dice pool, roll Foundation + Pillar (difficulty 7).\u201d</span> It's not the Dark Ages: Mage magic system; it's a hack designed to <i>simulate</i> the Dark Ages: Mage system using the powers described in Vampire's Disciplines. And that's why V20 DA leaves the door open to Pillar ratings above 5: Disciplines go all the way up to 10, so if you want a V20DA witch to be able to access powers granted by Discipline ratings of 6 or more you need to allow her to have Pillar ratings of 6 or more. <br /> <br /> Put in DA:Mage terms, the Pillars as described in V20DA don't follow the progression described in DA:Mage. One dot of V20DA Summer is not the same thing as one dot of DAM Summer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-23-2021, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T09:41:34-07:00","id":1376566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375238-archpillars-dark-age-archmages?p=1376562#post1376562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Foundation and Pillars system as described in V20 Dark Ages is a hack that's built on the framework of Vampire's Disciplines:</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's why I say &quot;<span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I suspect if the author has full understanding of DAM, Pillar system is very different from Spheres' and Disciplines'&quot;, just like Masters of the Art. Authors treat spheres like disciplines but that's wrong. So I think you shouldn't take this reference seriously</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 03-25-2020, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T09:58:36-07:00","id":1376573,"title":"","content":"It isn't \u201cwrong\u201d. It's \u201cdifferent\u201d. Specifically, what V20DA has in it is a simulation of Foundation and Pillars. A simulation does not work the same way as the actual system, not is it intended to; just similar enough to convey much of the same feel without having to spend pages and pages reproducing all of the original rules. <br /> <br /> But by the same token, you cannot glean any deep insights about the Foundation and Pillars system from the Foundation and Pillars simulation that V20DA features.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-25-2020, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T10:02:15-07:00","id":1376574,"title":"","content":"Well I am still of the feeling that Archspheres have a place in the game, even if the current headhoncho doesn't like them. And I feel Archpillars are also potentially a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T10:12:22-07:00","id":1376577,"title":"","content":"And that's fine; feel free to house-rule something for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T10:21:18-07:00","id":1376580,"title":"","content":"Still new to Dark Age Mage, so I especially don't know a lot of the era specific lore. Do the Fellowships have infamous Archmaster types? I forgot We have Taftani somewhere as a Fellowship right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T19:39:03-07:00","id":1376645,"title":"","content":"The other thing about Tome of Secrets is: What qualifies as 'legendary?' I mean are we talking a really famous archmage or something like the Wyck or Lilith (they could be 'legendary' mages too I think?) which to me kinda just reinforces the 'its optional' phrasing implied in that.<br /> <br /> Besides as another recent thread mentioned not everyone may like/agree with the Archsphere idea from Masters of the Art given that Horizon gave a similar/different approach. If you went the Horizon path and paired that with, say, Sorcerer revised and their approach to paths (also capping at ~6 dots IIRC) then it might be reasonable to assume Pillars/Foundations could cap at 6 (a wizard who might be able to affect an entire country/land with magic seems like it would fit at that scale. although I'm not sure upping the scale past that fits thematically with DA Mage except in really really rare cases.) <br /> <br /> Of course given some of the other abilities (and problems) ascribed to Archmages in MotA you might surmise that the limits are also location-dependent (The same way difficulties IIRC cant' go lower than 3-4 on earth, but could be lower elsewhere. Maybe the effective 'level' of a pillar or foundation might be higher off earth?) <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T08:07:34-07:00","id":1376715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375238-archpillars-dark-age-archmages?p=1376580#post1376580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I forgot We have Taftani somewhere as a Fellowship right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they're older than the Batini.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still new to Dark Age Mage, so I especially don't know a lot of the era specific lore. Do the Fellowships have infamous Archmaster types? </div> </div> </div>They <i>should </i>have, I think. But DA it's a short line and they weren't mentioned, not that I remember at least. Some old Archmasters of Ascencion would have been alive in the DA era, but I can't tell if they were Archmasters already, nor if they would aknowledge belonging to a Fellowship.<br /> <br /> Medea probably would count as that for the Old Faith<br /> <br /> If any of the founders of the OoH was alive back then, he/she would likely have that rank, but I think they died or vanished into the other worlds before the 13th century. <hr />One thing that must be mentioned about Archmastery in DA it's this: The title of &quot;Magister Mundi&quot;(9th degree), which it's the title that Archmasters are given in the OoH (as per Revised OoH Trad book, you need to have reached Archmastery to get it) it's granted to any mage with Modus 5 and it's 4 Pillars at 5 (as per the DA: Grimoire, which it's an actual book of Mage<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />A instead of an adaptation to Vampire).<br /> <br /> So, there's that: Archmastery in DA seem to be acknowledged to mages with their Foundation and pillars all at 5 (<i>or</i> <i>at least</i> <i>that</i>). This is consistent with Horizon: SoH, that has the first rules about Archspheres, <i>but doesn't consider them to be a requisite for Archmastery </i>(having 4 Spheres at 5 was the requisite for a mage to be aknowledged as Archmaster)<br /> <br /> Canon ArchPillars do not exist. But that's what house rules are for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T08:38:40-07:00","id":1376719,"title":"","content":"Very illuminating! I forgot about the you don't need Archspheres for the rank part!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T19:43:47-07:00","id":1376891,"title":"","content":"The implications of what Aleph mentions also illustrate that the Foundation/Pillar system is distinctly different (mechanically and not just flavor) from the sphere system which also can be a factor. Someone who might be exceptional enough to reach the level of 'Magister Mundi' might also be exceptional enough that they could learn the pillars/foundations of another mage and gain power a 'different' way. Since Foundation/Pillar rules allow you to use magic even if your Foundation is lower than your Pillar (at the cost of quintessence) you could see someone who might achieve alot of power in other ways. Indeed learning/practicing the arts of several (related) fellowships might be the sort of thing that lead to some exceptional being developing sphere magic (or some proto-sphere magic.. maybe a version of the 'minor' spheres optional rule.) Heck given that Mages Grimoire notes that the Ahl-i-Batin, Messianic voices, and Order of Hermes are all tied to Solomon one might surmise that Solomon is a good example of what a 'Dark Ages' Archmaster/mage might look like (which also leans something closer the Wyck or Lilith I think.) <br /> Isis perhaps might be considered another, although she might also be considered more on Lilith scale. <br /> <br /> Speculation: If we develop this further along the pillar/foundation route is it POSSIBLE to have more than four pillars 'at one time'? I know the Craftmasons (a derivative of the Order) had Materia but they still stayed with four pillars (they dropped Prime for Materia.) An Archmaster might be one who breaks the four-pillar limit (by picking up/integrating the arts of a different fellowship) and moves closer to a more 'Sphere-oriented' view of magic. <br /> <br /> Alternately (and equally possible) Archmasters/Archmages represent an entirely different/higher tier of Foundation/Pillar makeup (that is they have pillars and foundation, but they're more advanced (and more powerful) than what a 'normal' fellowship offers. Extraploating from the Charts in MtA like <a href=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/8/81/Cycle_of_Effect.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20151222155748\" target=\"_blank\">this one</a> off the Wiki you might surmise that forces/matter/life is one pillar, mind/spirit is another, correspondence/time is a third, and Prime/Entropy a fourth (although you could merge Entropy with Correspondence/Time as well, I think and leave a more developed idea of 'prime' as the fourth pillar if we were thinking of archmagic from a Hermetic view, lets say.) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T20:59:42-07:00","id":1376896,"title":"","content":"Very interesting ideas! Hmm developing new Pillars, I speculated on that with Fae Powers in Changeling them developing Arch Arts or Dominions rather then achieving Arts higher then 5, closer to Dark Age Fae powers, but well better defined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T14:40:25-07:00","id":1376997,"title":"","content":"Any Dark Ages Mage /can/ have more than 4 Pillars at a time, both In-Foundation as a Fellowship and Out-Foundation as a mage. Page 91 of DA:M's sidebar &quot;More Than Four?&quot; States that players can make new Pillars and implies that there are more than what we are given, but in honesty those Pillars are probably not utilized by many people but that more than 4 Pillars can exist in a Foundation. And Page 135-136 talks about how Mages can go learn Pillars from different Foundations, and while its hard it does allow them to learn new techniques. Probably though filtered through their own beliefs and Foundation, but still able to do that. There is no mention that I could find that states that you are only allowed 4 Pillars at any time. Experience wise, diversifying like that isn't very efficient, and as such probably not common in play. After all you can twist Pillars creatively just like Spheres with enough imagination for the effect and charisma for your Storyteller to allow it. I would think that in world however, its very uncommon to learn more than the four major Pillars, and rare to even want to learn other Pillars.<br /> I personally don't think they should be a thing, just like I don't think Archspheres should be a thing. Personally with Dark Ages Mage I think the more interesting (and cool) idea would be to go past Foundation 5. Now Im not the biggest whiz when it comes to mechanics, I tend to play a more narrative playstyle so mechanics are a more narrative thing, but Foundation seems to really be the core of a Fellowship. The Foundation is how the idea of magic itself is filtered through you, how you /believe/ magic to be, and how it changes you as you grow more powerful, hence the super cool and evocative bonuses they give as you grow. So while I have forgotten the exact bonuses Foundation gives, Archmastery for DA:M seems to be tied to Foundation rather than Pillars both in terms of raw power and magical connectedness.<br /> If Archpillars were to be a thing I'd make them more like Metamagic from D&amp;D, make it less of a dot tree and more like a point buy system that each dot gives you increasingly more points to buy magic modifications with, or enhancements for other modifications. So the dots themselves don't actually give you more abilities directly, instead representing the mage learning how to alter the manner in which their spells are expanding, showing &quot;mastery&quot; of that Pillar. But make it so that you can only use a certain amount of Meta-Pillar modifications based on Foundation, but lime using Pillars past your Foundation needs Quintessence, using Meta-Pillars should need Quintessence is your Foundation doesn't cover them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25226-knightfenrirwulfhart","user":"KnightFenrirWulfhart","date":".  Added possible Quintessence restrictions for Meta-Pillars 03-28-2020, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25226-knightfenrirwulfhart","name":"KnightFenrirWulfhart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T21:56:42-07:00","id":1377071,"title":"","content":"I mentioned Pillars from other foundations, which is one of the ways you might have Dark Ages 'archmaster' (someone who is on the cusp of realizing a proto-Sphere theory of magic basically, and perhaps has a way to cross-pollinate between diffrent fellowships). I did consider page 91's 'new pillar creation' sidebar but that carried more of the usual 'ST can do this but it's bad because its twink powergaming' discouragement that you get sprinkled throughout ST system games (including in other places in Dark Ages mage). The clear implication is that whilst you can do it, its not considered the 'right' way (which again gets back to the CraftMasons and their dropping prime for Materia, rather than retaining both)<br /> <br /> But in terms of 'optional rules' the idea that an Archmage/Archmaster might have more than four pillars is certainly another interesting way to explore the concept from a Foundation/Pillar perspective. As a synthesis of 'Mages learning foundation/pillars of other fellowships' you could have them 'reverse-engineer' another fellowship's foundations to develop an 'in-fellowship' variant. Hermetics for example could probably learn from the Ahl-I-Batin OR Messaianic Voices (The Batini seem a closer fit and one that complements the Hermetic weaknesses than the Voices do, but the Mithraic Voices seem like they might find a home in the Order of Hermes), or if you really wanted to consider you could have the Hermetics learning Old Faith or Valdarmen (more an 'opposites attract' sort of thing, but I feel this might be leading more towards 'forbidden knowledge.) The Ahl-I-Batin and the Voices being synthesized in on Mage is probably another 'opposites attract' (the Grimoire talks about Muslim voices as I recall)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375238-archpillars-dark-age-archmages?p=1376896#post1376896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very interesting ideas! Hmm developing new Pillars, I speculated on that with Fae Powers in Changeling them developing Arch Arts or Dominions rather then achieving Arts higher then 5, closer to Dark Age Fae powers, but well better defined.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting idea, but I'm not sure how well Changeling approaches to 'magic' translate to Mage. I just have this feeling that a 'mage' equivalent of Dominion and unleashing requires altering the local Consensus and this feels more like a situational thing - having places of power or areas on Earth where magic is strong/consensus is weak where vulgar stuff would still be coincidental (or something you would do off-earth.) To borrow an out-of-setting analogy I'd be thinking of a Chaos incursion (warp storm, warp rift) into the materium in Warhammer/Warhammer 40K terms where reality suddenly becomes more mutable. I always felt Dark Age Fae's approach to Fae powers was odd given CtD's arts and realms. Dominions I liked, but cantrips felt too much like linear/static magic or their analogues (Garou Gifts, Vampire Disciplines, etc.) rather than CtD cantrip (which feel like they occupy a middle ground between DA:fae cnatrips and unleashing Dominions). And thats without adding C20's approach to unleashings.<br /> <br /> But I suppose if you wanted to emulate it and felt ambitious you might find ways to tie static and dynamic magic together (and its not entirely impossible. See Sorcerer:Revised and the 'Struggling awake' merit which suggests the boundaries between static and dynamic magic aren't that rigid. Nevermind that ghoul mages, Kinfolk mages, and Kinain mages all reflectd examples of how Dynamic and static magic might overlap. V20's archaic sorcery from the Black Hand book had interesting ideas about how dynamic magic might handle 'vampiric' powers as coincidental which apply here too)<br /> <br /> (one thing I've been toying with which is semi-but-not related here has been looking at Mummy from 2nd and MtR and seeing if there might be a way to devise an 'archaic sorcery/Foundation pillar' approach for the cult of isis. Given Isis is/was a True Mage it seems like it would be appropriate for that. And Isis would be a source that ties both to the Hermetics AND 'old faith' in interesting ways but ALSO would be another potential 'archmaster' figure.) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","user":"Mister_Dunpeal","date":". 03-29-2020, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T22:05:14-07:00","id":1377073,"title":"","content":"Did Dark Age Mage every Address Sorcery? It kinda seemed sometimes Dark Age Mage diverged into two beings, Sorcerers and Sphere mages.<br /> <br /> On the topic of the Metamagic I always figured a Capstone Archpillar would work like that, making other effects easier. Or maybe borrowing from some Chronicles of Darkness idea of the Archpillar containing smart effects, so magic that would seem smart and ajust itself to the situation, like smart curses or blessings, rather then having to have the totality of all potential sideeffects determined in the casting the smart magic effect has the spell roll with the vicissitudes of conditions changing with time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T22:13:16-07:00","id":1377079,"title":"","content":"I'm not against new Pillars; but to my mind, they're not something that individuals create: it takes a Fellowship to create them, or at least a significant portion of a Fellowship's Masters. It may even be part and parcel of the founding of a <i>new</i> Fellowship, the way the Craftmasons traded out Primus for Materia when they formed. Limiting it to four Pillars per Fellowship also means that a mage who raised his Foundation to 5 gets to work without tools for all of them; adding a fifth means that even a Master can't *ahem* master them all. <br /> <br /> But if anyone could create new Pillars on their own or matter more than four Pillars, it would be an Archmaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T22:15:29-07:00","id":1377082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375238-archpillars-dark-age-archmages?p=1377073#post1377073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did Dark Age Mage every Address Sorcery? It kinda seemed sometimes Dark Age Mage diverged into two beings, Sorcerers and Sphere mages.</div> </div> </div> </div> Dark Ages: Mage never addressed sorcery; that was left to Dark Ages: Vampire. But remember that DAM was originally published as a supplement for DAV; so if DAV addressed it, it was available for DAM too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"No